{"G1067":{"id":"G1067","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1067","disambiguated_id":"G1067 =","unique_id":"G1067","headword":"γέεννα","transliteration":"geenna","lexical_morphology":"N:N--T","gloss_en":"hell: Gehenna","definition_en":"γέεννα (γέενα, Mrk.9:45, Rec.), -ης, ἡ (perh. through Aram. גֵּיהִנָּם, from Heb. גֵּי הִנֹּם, Neh.11:30; גֵּי בֶּן־הִנֹּם, Jhn.18:16; גֵּי בּנֵי־הִנֹּם, 4Ki.23:10; valley of (the son, sons of) lamentation); \n [in LXX the nearest approach to γ. is γαίεννα, Jos.18:16 (Γαὶ Ὀννόμ, A), elsewhere φάραγξ Ὀνόμ (Jos.15:8, al.), V. Swete on Mrk.9:43 ;] \nGehenna, a valley W. and S. of Jerusalem, which as the site of fire-worship from the time of Ahaz, was desecrated by Josiah and became a dumping-place for the offal of the city. Later, the name was used as a symbol of the place of future punishment, as in NT: Mat.5:29, ; 10:28, Mrk.9:43, 45 47, Luk.12:5, Jas.3:6; γ. τ. πυρός, Mat.5:22 18:19, prob. with ref. to fires of Moloch (DB, ii, 119b); υἱὸς γεέννης, Mat.23:15; κρίσις γεέννης, 23:33.†\n (AS)","source_line":1193}],"occurrence_count":12,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"inferno","count":11},{"gloss":"da-geena","count":1}]},"G1708":{"id":"G1708","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1708","disambiguated_id":"G1708 =","unique_id":"G1708","headword":"ἐμπλοκή","transliteration":"emplokē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"braiding","definition_en":"ἐμ-πλοκή, ῆς, ἡ\n (ἐμπλίκω), \na braiding: τριχῶν, 1Pe.3:3.†\n (AS)","source_line":1849}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"de-tranças","count":1}]},"G2156":{"id":"G2156","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2156","disambiguated_id":"G2156 =","unique_id":"G2156","headword":"εὐσχημόνως","transliteration":"euschēmonōs","lexical_morphology":"G:ADV","gloss_en":"properly","definition_en":"εὐσχημόνως \n adv. (εὐσχήμων), \ndecorously, becomingly: 1Co.14:40; περιπατεῖν, Rom.13:13, 1Th.4:12.†\n (AS)","source_line":2298}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed